{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Task Cancellation Tokens.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Task Cancellation Tokens.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"task cancellation tokens task cancellation tokens","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Task Cancellation Tokens.md","fileName":"Task Cancellation Tokens.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Task Cancellation Tokens","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 00:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Task Cancellation Tokens.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Task Cancellation Tokens.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"task cancellation tokens task cancellation tokens","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Task Cancellation Tokens.md","fileName":"Task Cancellation Tokens.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Task Cancellation Tokens","heading":"Task Cancellation Tokens","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A `CancellationTokenSource` issues a cooperative cancellation request, and its token lets operations poll the request or register a callback. Passing the same token through a task graph gives callers a consistent way to state that unfinished work is no longer needed.\n\nCancellation does not forcibly stop arbitrary code. The operation must reach a safe observation point, release resources, and report cancellation distinctly from failure. This cooperation preserves invariants that abrupt thread termination could leave broken.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Task Parallelism and Asynchrony","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Task Canc